{"id":"f476670b-c8fa-484d-9a2c-440386724468","object":"chat.completion","created":1784834268,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    dist_list = case['distances']\\n    # validate nodes\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n not in core:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing core_distance for node {n}\\\")\\n    # build distance lookup\\n    dist_dict = {}\\n    for a, b, d in dist_list:\\n        key = tuple(sorted((a, b)))\\n        if key in dist_dict:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Duplicate distance entry for {a},{b}\\\")\\n        dist_dict[key] = d\\n    # check all node pairs present\\n    node_set = set(nodes)\\n    for i in range(len(nodes)):\\n        for j in range(i+1, len(nodes)):\\n            key = (nodes[i], nodes[j])\\n            if key not in dist_dict:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing distance for pair {key}\\\")\\n    # build mutual reachability edges\\n    edges = []\\n    for (u, v), d in dist_dict.items():\\n        w = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    # sort deterministically: weight, then u, then v (u<v already)\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\\n    # union-find\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is not connected\\\")\\n    return {\\\"edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source code for solve(case). The function must compute core distances, mutual-reachability edge weights, and a minimum spanning tree using Kruskal with deterministic tie-breaking. Input: case has 'nodes' (list of node IDs), 'core_distance' (dict mapping node to float), 'distances' (list of [node1, node2, distance]). Output: JSON-serializable object with fields like \"edges\" (list of edges with source, target, weight?), \"total_weight\". Also need to validate. Use only standard library. No mutation of case.\n\nSteps:\n1. Validate inputs: nodes exist, core_distance for each node, distances cover all pairs? Actually distances may not be complete? But we need mutual reachability for all node pairs? The problem says \"for each pair compute mutual reachability\". But the distances list may not include all pairs? The fixtures show 10 distances for 5 nodes (complete graph). So we assume all pairs are provided. If missing, raise ValueError.\n2. Build a dict of distances: key (u,v) sorted tuple, value distance.\n3. For each unordered pair (i,j) with i<j, compute mutual reachability = max(core_distance[i], core_distance[j], distance). Use the distance from distances list.\n4. Build list of edges: (weight, source, target) where source and target are node IDs. Tie-breaking: sort by weight, then by source, then by target (canonicalized: smaller node ID first? canonicalize undirected endpoints: sort the node IDs so that source < target).\n5. Run Kruskal's algorithm using union-find (DSU). Deterministic: when edges have same weight, sort by source, then target. Use a list of edges sorted accordingly.\n6. Check that the graph is connected: after processing, number of selected edges = len(nodes)-1. If not, raise ValueError.\n7. Return dict: edges list (each edge as [source, target, weight]), total_weight (sum of selected edge weights). Also maybe include core_distances? But spec says \"Return only JSON-serializable values with the exact named fields.\" The candidate artifact mentions \"selected edges plus total weight\". Probably return {\"edges\": [...], \"total_weight\": float}. Also need to include \"mutual_reachability\" edges? The spec says \"Compute mutual-reachability edge weights\" but output is MST. So output likely MST edges and total weight.\n\nDouble-check: \"Return selected edges plus total weight.\" Yes.\n\nAlso need to validate that core_distance is present for each node, distances list contains all pairs? Not explicitly but if missing pair, we can't compute mutual reachability. We'll raise ValueError if any pair missing.\n\nImplement DSU with path compression and union by rank.\n\nTie-breaking: sort edges by (weight, node1, node2) where node1 < node2.\n\nImplementation details: Use tuples, sort.\n\nReturn dict with keys \"edges\" (list of [source, target, weight]) and \"total_weight\" (float).\n\nEnsure no mutation of case.\n\nWrite solve(case) function.\n\nNow produce JSON with escaped string.\n\nMake sure no extra whitespace.\n\nWe'll produce the JSON object directly.\n\nImplementation string must be valid Python.\n\nLet's produce the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1656,"completion_tokens":1324,"total_tokens":2980,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":695},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":120},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}